    "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #44189\n\n`/start_profile` takes `profile_prefix` and `profile_id` from the caller and joins them into the trace filename as is. a prefix like `../escaped` writes the trace one level above `output_dir`; an absolute prefix like `/tmp/elsewhere/x` makes `os.path.join` drop `output_dir` entirely. `profile_id` has the same problem.\n\n(#44201 tried this but was closed along with everything else from that account.)\n\n## Modifications\n\n- add `sanitize_profile_filename_component` in `profile_utils.py`; it replaces `/`, `\\`, `os.sep`, `os.altsep` and NUL with `_` and leaves everything else alone, so normal ids and prefixes keep their exact names\n- call it on `profile_id` and `profile_prefix` at the top of `ProfilerManager.configure`, so both the v1 path and the `SGLANG_PROFILE_V2` path get clean values (this also covers the memory snapshot and merged trace names that reuse them)\n- call it on `profile_prefix` in the encoder profiler too\n\nwith no separators left, the joined name is always a single filename under `output_dir`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nn/a; no model code changed.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nn/a\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests: `test/registered/unit/managers/test_profile_filename_sanitize.py` checks relative, absolute and `profile_id` escapes stay inside `output_dir`, and that plain values are unchanged; passes on cpu.\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41185613016](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41185613016)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41185612950](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41185612950)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41185612979](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41185612979)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
